Use an authorized complete edition for further sustained study of biological/chemical coupling, methods, reactor and field contexts, practical observations, and environmental applications. Read whole chapters and the complete primary methods actually used in a bioleaching study; distinguish biological effects from changes in solution chemistry, surface state, and mass transport.

The indexed official catalogue verifies editors, title, and year. One direct announcement request timed out; successful complete-text inspection or laboratory execution is not claimed. Preserve actual book/component notices and verify authorized availability for the edition used. This optional book complements the public extraction-course and primary-study progression. No book, culture data, or laboratory media is bundled.

